{
  "requirement": "When `habeas status` or `habeas status --all` displays a Markdown table, it MUST left-align and space-pad the Definition and Evidence columns so every row, including the header and separator row, has its `|` column delimiters in the same positions. Column widths MUST be determined by the widest displayed cell in each column.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation.** `render_evidence_table` in `src/markdown.rs` (lines 1–~35) computes each column width as the maximum cell length. It includes the header literals \"Definition\" and \"Evidence\" in that maximum. It then uses `{:<width$}` left-aligned padding for the header row, the `---` separator row and every data row. Every row therefore has its `|` delimiters in the same positions, and the widths come from the widest displayed cell.\n\n`.len()` is a byte count, not a display width. That is safe here because definition names are restricted to ASCII (`valid_name` in `src/lib.rs` allows only ASCII alphanumerics, `_` and `-`, plus `.` separators). The rest of each cell is the backticked name and a fixed ASCII kind noun. Evidence labels are also fixed ASCII strings.\n\n**Wiring.** `status_markdown_with_options` in `src/commands.rs` (~line 96) renders its rows through this function. The same function serves both `habeas status` and `habeas status --all`, since `all` only changes which rows are collected. The index page (`src/index.rs` ~line 351) uses it too.\n\n**Tests.** `status_tables_align_each_column_to_its_widest_cell` in `tests/commands.rs` is tagged `{test}` for this requirement. It runs both `status` and `status --all` against a fixture with rows of varying widths. For each run it:\n- extracts the table lines;\n- asserts that every line has the same three pipe positions as the header;\n- asserts that each cell has exactly one leading space, so content is left-aligned;\n- asserts that each column's width equals its widest trimmed content, plus the surrounding padding;\n- asserts that the separator row cells are `---`.\n\nThis covers both command forms, the header and separator rows, left alignment, and widest-cell sizing. The empty-rows case prints a message instead of a table, so it needs no alignment test. I found no acknowledged gaps or FIXMEs.",
  "inputs": [
